{"name":"Wulfenite","hex":"#ce7639","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wulfenite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An orange mineral, lead molybdate, PbMoO4, found in lead veins."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wulfenite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wulfenite","blocks":[{"text":"Wulfenite is a lead molybdate mineral with the formula PbMoO4. It often occurs as thin tabular crystals with a bright orange-red to yellow-orange color, sometimes brown, although the color can be highly variable. In its yellow form it is sometimes called \"yellow lead ore\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Wulfenite_-_Red_Cloud_mine%2C_La_Paz_Co.%2C_Arizona%2C_USA.jpg/330px-Wulfenite_-_Red_Cloud_mine%2C_La_Paz_Co.%2C_Arizona%2C_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wulfenite"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Wulfenite-251130.jpg/250px-Wulfenite-251130.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Wulfenite-251130.jpg/330px-Wulfenite-251130.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Wulfenite-251130.jpg/250px-Wulfenite-251130.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWulfenite-251130.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Wulfenite-43291.jpg/250px-Wulfenite-43291.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Wulfenite-43291.jpg/330px-Wulfenite-43291.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Wulfenit